framework ArchitectureDecisionRecord:
  requires problem and decision
  requires premise and evidence
  warns pending

domain ADR0030:
  description "ADR-0030 revision 1: Versioned LLM-assisted character semantic migration. Status Accepted."

problem P1:
  |
    Eight exact ready V2 character generations are excluded from new matches
    after V2 action-norm meaning was tightened. Accepted requirement revision 6
    requires migration to strict immutable V3 without a permanent V2 reader,
    deterministic-only dead end, unrestricted rewrite, or read-time provider call.

premise AUTHORITY:
  |
    Accepted ADR-0010 owns immutable generations, persisted attempts, readiness,
    CAS activation, and read-only battle binding. ADR-0011 owns structured
    character truth and compiler-specific projections. ADR-0027 and ADR-0028 own
    conscious judgment, reaction-only psyche, and existing qualified runtime V3
    identities. Accepted requirement revision 6 authorizes this proposal but not
    its acceptance, implementation, provider use, deployment, or production work.

premise IDENTITIES:
  |
    Bare V3 is already used by BattleAssetManifest schema 3,
    CharacterBattleCompilerInputsV3, dialogue schema 3, conscious I/O 3, and
    CharacterAgentState.consciousAgencyV1. New contracts need qualified names and
    cannot silently change any of those meanings.

evidence E_INCIDENT:
  |
    The audited character authoring and selection RCA records nine exact current
    ready V2 generations, eight rejected by invalid_action_norm_selector with
    twenty-one selectorless soft entries, and Takumi remaining selectable. Sixteen
    owner characters have no exact ready V2 state and are outside the operation.

evidence E_REQUIREMENT:
  |
    docs/character-v2-compatibility-requirements-v6.md R1-R25 and its exact owner
    acceptance select bounded LLM-assisted semantic change sets, preservation,
    consumer-scoped deferral, whole-candidate semantic review, bounded repair,
    owner acceptance, append-only per-asset activation, and explicit cutover.

evidence E_REJECTED:
  |
    ADR-0029 revision 2 records the permanent V2 compatibility-reader proposal as
    Rejected. Historical V2 bytes and battle bindings remain readable, but no new
    match-selection exception is introduced.

premise OPTIONS:
  |
    A retain a permanent V2 reader. B use deterministic mapping only. C let one
    unrestricted LLM response rewrite and activate. D use a versioned hybrid:
    deterministic exact copy, bounded LLM semantic operations, deterministic
    enforcement, independent semantic review, owner acceptance, and append/CAS.

evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    On 2026-09-10, after the exact English authoritative think, its Markdown
    projection, and the complete Japanese review scope were presented with the
    purpose, differences, decision points, alternatives, risks, and unknowns,
    the product owner replied ACCEPT for exact ADR-0030 revision 1.

decision D1 based_on P1, AUTHORITY, E_INCIDENT, E_REQUIREMENT, E_REJECTED, OPTIONS:
  |
    Propose option D. Refine ADR-0010 and ADR-0011 only for versioned character
    semantic migration and schema-3 authoring. Preserve their immutable history,
    validation, confirmation, CAS, read-only binding, and no-provider-in-activation
    invariants. Preserve ADR-0027 and ADR-0028 runtime responsibility boundaries.

decision D2 based_on D1, IDENTITIES, E_REQUIREMENT:
  |
    Add CharacterDefinitionV3. It contains strict executable actionNorms and a
    separate bounded CharacterConsciousGuidanceV1 collection. Every actionNorm has
    at least one actionRef, actionKind, or tacticTag. Conscious guidance has stable
    ID, applicability, statement, priority, preference-or-commitment force,
    self-awareness, exceptions, and descriptive metadata, but no action selector,
    restrictive disposition, tactic, or fallback action.

decision D3 based_on D2, IDENTITIES, E_REQUIREMENT:
  |
    A migrated mechanical fallback uses CharacterMechanicalConflictFallbackV1,
    with qualified applicability, ordered registered action references, legality
    revalidation, and a conflict receipt. V3 battle compilation outputs
    CharacterBattleCompilerInputsV4 and uses basic-action provenance discriminator
    character_generation_v3. Existing V2/V3 names retain their current meanings.

decision D4 based_on D2, D3, E_REQUIREMENT:
  |
    Define CharacterCompilerCapabilitySetV1 as registered qualified consumer and
    compiler requirements. Optional unresolved values are represented in a
    separate bounded CharacterDeferredValueV1 collection with target path, reason,
    candidate source paths, and requiring capability. Active definition fields do
    not contain sentinel strings. Compatibility reports supported, blocked, and
    deferred qualified capabilities; only a required affected capability blocks.

decision D5 based_on D2, D3, D4, E_REQUIREMENT:
  |
    Store MigrationPreservationCapsuleV1 in a dedicated restricted persistence
    record keyed by content digest and bound to source and target generation IDs.
    It is not inside CharacterDefinitionV3 and no ordinary public, battle, psyche,
    conscious, narration, image, or authoring compiler can load it. It contains
    exact displaced paths and canonical values plus operation provenance, is
    limited to 256 KiB per character, and is retained with the referenced
    generations. Export or deletion follows the logical asset's existing owner
    data lifecycle; only a registered future migration consumer may read it.

decision D6 based_on D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, E_REQUIREMENT:
  |
    CharacterSemanticMigrationContractV1 freezes one migrationAttemptId over the
    complete source, permitted natural source, target schema, prompt, response
    schema, provider route, model, compiler capabilities, and initial request
    digest. Each invocation has a distinct providerRequestId, parent request,
    request digest, accounting record, and response or failure receipt. Candidate,
    target generation, and current pointer identities remain separate.

decision D7 based_on D6, E_REQUIREMENT:
  |
    The response identity character_semantic_migration_change_set_v1 returns only
    copy, move, transform, synthesize, retire_to_capsule, and defer operations.
    Operations identify target, registered source paths, value or deferred marker,
    bounded owner explanation, provenance category, and proposed semantic
    dependants. Server code allocates stable IDs and rejects invented control IDs,
    runtime facts, information rights, or undisclosed mechanics.

decision D8 based_on D6, D7, E_REQUIREMENT:
  |
    Server structural validation computes registered dependencies. A stateless
    CharacterSemanticConsistencyReviewV1 request receives the frozen source,
    complete merged candidate, contract, and declared operations, but not hidden
    model reasoning or conversational state. It may use the same accepted provider
    and model but is a separately receipted request. Repair closure is the union of
    structural dependencies, proposed semantic dependants, and reviewer findings.

decision D9 based_on D8, E_REQUIREMENT:
  |
    Permit at most two repair rounds after the initial generation. Each round has
    one bounded CharacterSemanticRepairV1 request followed by one fresh complete-
    candidate semantic review. Thus one attempt has at most six provider requests:
    initial generation, initial review, two repair requests, and two re-reviews.
    A separately accepted execution ceiling may be lower but never higher without
    a new ADR revision. Every merge receives full structural revalidation.

decision D10 based_on D6, D7, D8, D9, E_REQUIREMENT:
  |
    Persist attempts, provider requests, candidates, capsules, owner acceptances,
    and success receipts in dedicated append-oriented records. A completed attempt
    replays without provider work or duplicate generation. Requested semantic
    regeneration creates a new attempt. Provider failure, invalid output, decline,
    source drift, or pointer drift leaves the current generation unchanged.

decision D11 based_on D10, AUTHORITY, E_REQUIREMENT:
  |
    Per asset, one transaction appends the accepted V3 envelope, capsule binding,
    compatibility state and success receipt, then CAS-moves the current pointer
    from the frozen source. Assets commit independently. Existing V2 generations
    and old battle bindings remain byte-readable. Rollback CAS-moves only an
    affected current pointer to a previously compatible generation and records a
    new receipt; it never deletes the V3 generation or capsule.

decision D12 based_on D2, D4, D10, D11, AUTHORITY, E_REQUIREMENT:
  |
    Store characterDefinitionSchemaVersion in a dedicated revisioned
    CharacterAuthoringPolicyV1 record with values 2 or 3 and CAS activation. It is
    not a wall-clock, deployment, dialogue-schema, or environment-variable
    default. Deploy and verify dual V2/V3 readers and migration resume before
    selecting 3. After selecting 3, create and ordinary revision emit strict V3;
    restore, import, derived, and historical upgrade use migration. Policy does not
    automatically downgrade during per-asset rollback; a later policy reversal
    requires a new accepted decision.

decision D13 based_on D1, D6, D9, D10, D11, D12, OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    After exact owner acceptance, implement the accepted successor plan B3-B7
    locally with focused tests, full test/type/build/duplication/Lizard gates, and
    Seal impact review. Deployment, provider-backed production generation,
    candidate acceptance, pointer migration, and policy activation retain their
    separate B8-B14 gates.

decision ACCEPTANCE based_on OWNER_ACCEPTANCE, D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D6, D7, D8, D9, D10, D11, D12, D13:
  |
    Accept exact ADR-0030 revision 1 and authorize its local successor-plan B3-B7
    implementation gates. Provider calls, deployment, production reads or writes,
    candidate acceptance, pointer movement, rollback, and authoring-policy
    activation remain separately authorized B8-B14 effects.
